{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-159658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the chain rule: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{2xy-1}) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the sum and the constant multiple rules for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy-1) & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}(2x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\cdot (2x\\cdot 1-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-159658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{2x\\sqrt{2xy-1}}"] ["math" "-\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}"] ["math" "\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y)={e}^{xy}+{x}^{2}y,$ evaluate ${f}_{y}(1,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy}+{x}^{2}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the chain and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y) & ={e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)+{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}\\cdot x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)+{x}^{2}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =x{e}^{xy}\\cdot (1)+{x}^{2} \\\\  & =x{e}^{xy}+{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,0):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,0) & =1\\cdot {e}^{1\\cdot 0}+{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-35718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "e"] ["math" "e+1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy),$ evaluate ${f}_{x}(\\frac{\\pi }{4},2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the chain and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\cdot (2x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot y\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =2x{y}^{2}+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(\\frac{\\pi }{4},2) & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot {2}^{2}+2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =2\\pi +2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =2\\pi +2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-159660" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159660" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\pi +1"] ["math" "2\\pi +2"] ["math" "4\\pi "] ["math" "\\pi +2"] ["math" "\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159660" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\pi +2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35713" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ for $f(x,y)=(x+1)^{{y}^{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35713" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the chain rule: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((x+1)^{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the sum rule for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+1) & ={y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\cdot (\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\cdot (1+0) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35713" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-35713" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35713" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x+1)^{{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)"] ["math" "2(x+1)^{{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)"] ["math" "2y(x+1)^{2y-1}"] ["math" "y(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}"] ["math" "{y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35713" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)={e}^{{x}^{2}y}-y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{{x}^{2}y}-y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{{x}^{2}y})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the chain and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{{x}^{2}y})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}y}\\cdot y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})-y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}y}\\cdot y\\cdot 2x-y\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =2xy{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{y}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159656" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-159656" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159656" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2xy{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{y}{x}"] ["math" "2x{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "2y{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "xy{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{2y}{x}"] ["math" "{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{y}{x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159656" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2xy{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{y}{x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159768" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y)=xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(2,\\pi ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159768" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) & =x(\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y))+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\  & =x(1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+y\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y))+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\  & =x(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,\\pi ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(2,\\pi )} & =2\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi  \\\\  & =2(-1-\\pi \\cdot 0)+(-1) \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159768" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-159768" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159768" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-3+\\pi "] ["math" "1-\\pi "] ["math" "2-3\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159768" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y)=y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},$ evaluate ${f}_{y}(2,\\sqrt{5}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)\\cdot \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the chain, the sum, and the constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)\\cdot \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) & =1\\cdot \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+y\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot ({x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(1)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot ({x}^{2}\\cdot 0+2y) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,\\sqrt{5}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(2,\\sqrt{5})} & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}}+\\frac{{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+5}+\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{4+5}} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{5}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-159766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{11}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{14}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{14}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y)=y{e}^{xy}-{x}^{2}{y}^{2},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(1,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{xy}-{x}^{2}{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{xy})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{xy})-{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product, the chain, and the constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{xy})-{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}) & =(\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)\\cdot {e}^{xy}+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy}))-{x}^{2}\\cdot (2y) \\\\  & =(1\\cdot {e}^{xy}+y\\cdot {e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy))-2{x}^{2}y \\\\  & =({e}^{xy}+y\\cdot {e}^{xy}\\cdot x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y))-2{x}^{2}y \\\\  & =({e}^{xy}+y\\cdot {e}^{xy}\\cdot x\\cdot 1)-2{x}^{2}y \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}+xy{e}^{xy}-2{x}^{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(1,1)} & ={e}^{1\\cdot 1}+1\\cdot 1\\cdot {e}^{1\\cdot 1}-2\\cdot {1}^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =e+e-2 \\\\  & =2e-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-159751" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159751" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "2e+1"] ["math" "2e-2"] ["math" "3e"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159751" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2e-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+x\\sqrt{y},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(\\frac{1}{4},4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+x\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))+\\sqrt{y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product, the chain, and the constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))+\\sqrt{y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) & =(\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)))+\\sqrt{y}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =(1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+x\\cdot \\frac{1}{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy))+\\sqrt{y} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x))+\\sqrt{y} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+1+\\sqrt{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\frac{1}{4},4):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(1/4,4)} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4)+1+\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+1+2 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-159752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ for $f(x,y)={x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x{y}^{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) & =(\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4})\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x))-{y}^{3}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =((4{x}^{3})\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{x}^{4}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x))-{y}^{3} \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-159716" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159716" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{y}^{3}"] ["math" "4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{y}^{3}"] ["math" "{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x{y}^{3}"] ["math" "{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{y}^{3}"] ["math" "{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x{y}^{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159716" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{y}^{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(0,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)\\cdot (y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(0,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(0,2)} & =\\frac{2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-0\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}{(2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+0}{(2+0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-159709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159700" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x+y}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159700" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x+y}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+y)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡y-(x+y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)}{{sin}^{2}⁡y} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡y-(x+y)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{{sin}^{2}⁡y} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{{sin}^{2}⁡y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(\\pi ,\\pi /2)} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-0}{{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159700" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-159700" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159700" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\pi "] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159700" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2x{y}^{2}-1}{{x}^{2}y}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{2h(x,y)}{{x}^{3}y}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{2x{y}^{2}-1}{{x}^{2}y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2}-1)\\cdot {x}^{2}y-(2x{y}^{2}-1)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)}{({x}^{2}y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{y}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}y-(2x{y}^{2}-1)\\cdot 2xy}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}{y}^{3}-4{x}^{2}{y}^{3}+2xy}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy-2{x}^{2}{y}^{3}}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy(1-x{y}^{2})}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-x{y}^{2})}{{x}^{3}y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=1-x{y}^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159714" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-159714" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159714" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1+xy"] ["math" "1-x{y}^{2}"] ["math" "2-xy"] ["math" "2-y"] ["math" "3+{x}^{2}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159714" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1-x{y}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159713" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{3x+y}{\\sqrt{x+y}}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{h(x,y)}{2(x+y)\\sqrt{x+y}}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159713" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient and chain rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{3x+y}{\\sqrt{x+y}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3x+y)\\cdot \\sqrt{x+y}-(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{x+y})}{{(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3\\cdot \\sqrt{x+y}-(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+y}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+y))}{{(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3\\cdot \\sqrt{x+y}-(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+y}}\\cdot 1)}{{(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{6(x+y)-(3x+y)}{2\\sqrt{x+y}})}{x+y} \\\\  & =\\frac{3x+5y}{2(x+y)\\sqrt{x+y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=3x+5y.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159713" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-159713" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159713" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3x+5y"] ["math" "3y"] ["math" "4y-3x"] ["math" "5x"] ["math" "x-y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159713" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x+5y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{x-{y}^{2}}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{h(x,y)}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{x-{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot (x-{y}^{2})-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(x-{y}^{2})}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y\\cdot (x-{y}^{2})-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot (-2y)}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy-2{y}^{3}+2{x}^{2}y+2{y}^{3}}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy+2{x}^{2}y}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy(1+x)}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=2xy(1+x).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-159723" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159723" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2-x{y}^{2}"] ["math" "2xy(1+x)"] ["math" "2xy(1-y)"] ["math" "3+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}"] ["math" "x(2x+y)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-159723" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2xy(1+x)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-132253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y,z)=y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(3,-1,-2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-132253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the constant multiple and chain rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2})}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}{({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2})}^{-1/2})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}) & =\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{z}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\cdot (2x+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(3,-1,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(3,-1,-2)} & =\\frac{(3)(-1)}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+4(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{9+16}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-132253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-132253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-132253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-132253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz),$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(1,0,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xz)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})-(0) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot (2y) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(1,0,1)} & =2(1)^{2}(0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-35710" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35710" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35710" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-64907" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y,z)=xyz-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz),$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(1,0,\\pi ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-64907" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)) \\\\  & =yz\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)) \\\\  & =yz\\cdot 1-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)) \\\\  & =yz-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}yz-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz)) & =yz-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz) \\\\  & =yz-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz)\\cdot (z) \\\\  & =yz-z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz) \\\\  & =z(y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,0,\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(1,0,\\pi )} & =\\pi (0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot \\pi )) \\\\  & =\\pi (0-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-64907" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-64907" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-64907" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\pi "] ["math" "-\\pi "] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2\\pi "] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-64907" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-86812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y,z)={z}^{2}{e}^{xy}-{y}^{2}{e}^{yz},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}$ at the point $(0,-1,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-86812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $z,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2}{e}^{xy}-{y}^{2}{e}^{yz}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2}{e}^{xy})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{2}{e}^{yz}) \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2})-{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{yz})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2})-{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{yz}) & ={e}^{xy}\\cdot 2z-{y}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{yz}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz) \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}\\cdot 2z-{y}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{yz}\\cdot y \\\\  & =2z{e}^{xy}-{y}^{3}{e}^{yz}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(0,-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂z}{|}_{(0,-1,1)} & =2(1){e}^{(0)(-1)}-(-1)^{3}{e}^{(-1)(1)} \\\\  & =2+{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-86812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-86812" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-86812" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1+e"] ["math" "1-{e}^{-1}"] ["math" "2+e"] ["math" "2+{e}^{-1}"] ["math" "{e}^{-2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-86812" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2+{e}^{-1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${g}_{z}(x,y,z)$ for $g(x,y,z)=(x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+(z+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $z,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the sum and constant multiple rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}((x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+(z+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}((x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}((z+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =(x+y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡z)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}(z+y) \\\\  & =(x+y)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ca32964fbf092a924f2e3c05159ea4131887c6f8bd458df45eec7ec940121ef9"} {"question" "q-35721" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35721" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z"] ["math" "(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z-(z+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "(x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "(x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "q-35721" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ff763fdcab30a39035e009fbf62ed03d4b4b1799aa1fdb4003610e075c46487"} {"question" "e-11048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y) =\\ln(y-x^2),$ evaluate $f_x(1,9).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/example-11048.json" "file_sha256" "7e8c7140306fb9e32cf83b258ca5279043f1e23ed343c1e88364d8c684119034"} {"question" "e-11048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-{x}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-{x}^{2}) & =\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}}\\cdot (y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y-{x}^{2}}\\cdot (y\\cdot 0-2x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{y-{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,9)\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,9) & =-\\frac{2\\cdot 1}{9-{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/example-11048.json" "file_sha256" "7e8c7140306fb9e32cf83b258ca5279043f1e23ed343c1e88364d8c684119034"} {"question" "e-11028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ for $f(x,y) =x^2y\\ln{x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/example-11028.json" "file_sha256" "12ab36c209bc708841009466fdd7d1eb497447bac746e7e13d7581a1735c07c8"} {"question" "e-11028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the constant multiple rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) & =y\\cdot (\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)) \\\\  & =y\\cdot ((2x)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x})) \\\\  & =y(2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x) \\\\  & =xy(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/example-11028.json" "file_sha256" "12ab36c209bc708841009466fdd7d1eb497447bac746e7e13d7581a1735c07c8"} {"question" "e-11112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{4x-y}{x+y^2},$ evaluate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ at the point $(2,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/example-11112.json" "file_sha256" "c383fb1a197a48cd39117806fd9edfe34d63c27dcf42e05af66d5d0c3d82bac2"} {"question" "e-11112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{4x-y}{x+{y}^{2}}) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4x-y)\\cdot (x+{y}^{2})-(4x-y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+{y}^{2})}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot (x+{y}^{2})-(4x-y)\\cdot 1}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4x+4{y}^{2}-4x+y}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{y}^{2}+y}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,-1)\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(2,-1)} & =\\frac{4(-1)^{2}+(-1)}{{(2+{(-1)}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-1}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/example-11112.json" "file_sha256" "c383fb1a197a48cd39117806fd9edfe34d63c27dcf42e05af66d5d0c3d82bac2"} {"question" "e-11027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the function  $g(x,y,z) = 2 (x + 1)e^z+ yz,$  evaluate  $\\dfrac{\\partial g}{\\partial z}$ at $(1,1,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/example-11027.json" "file_sha256" "e0f34db64707ea1ba658ab2c1062547ec6a9722f02f08281dd1d1b1dbdad010a"} {"question" "e-11027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate the given function with respect to $z,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2(x+1){e}^{z}+yz) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2(x+1){e}^{z})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz) \\\\  & =2(x+1)\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{z})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz) \\\\  & =2(x+1){e}^{z}+y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,1,1)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂z}{|}_{(1,1,1)} & =2(1+1){e}^{1}+1 \\\\  & =4e+1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043339/example-11027.json" "file_sha256" "e0f34db64707ea1ba658ab2c1062547ec6a9722f02f08281dd1d1b1dbdad010a"}] "usage" {"e-11048" [] "q-35718" [] "e-11112" [] "q-159751" [] "e-11028" [] "e-11027" [] "q-35710" []} "basis" 1610 "retractions" [[17592186193148 :question/problem "For the function $f(x, y) = e^{xy} + x^{2}y$, evaluate $f_{y}(1, 0)$."] [17592186193024 :question/problem "For the function $f(x, y) = ye^{xy} - x^{2}y^{2}$, evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(1, 1)$."] [17592186193147 :question/problem "For the function $f(x, y, z) = x^{2}y^{2} - \\ln (xz)$, evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(1, 0, 1)$."] [17592186192341 :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y) =\\ln(y-x^2)$, evaluate $f_x(1,9)$."] [17592186192341 :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x$, treating all other variables as constants.\n\nFirst, we use the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{x}(x, y) &= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\ln (y - x^{2})) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{y - x^{2}} \\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(y - x^{2})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{y - x^{2}} \\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(y - x^{2}) &= \\frac{1}{y - x^{2}} \\cdot (y \\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(1) - \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2})) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{y - x^{2}} \\cdot (y \\cdot 0 - 2x) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2x}{y - x^{2}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,9)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{x}(1, 9) &= -\\frac{2 \\cdot 1}{9 - 1^{2}} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{8} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186192336 :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ for $f(x,y) =x^2y\\ln{x}$."] [17592186192336 :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x$, treating all other variables as constants.\n\nFirst, we use the constant multiple rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &= \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2}y\\ln x) \\\\\n&= y \\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2}\\ln x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny \\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2}\\ln x) &= y \\cdot (\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2}) \\cdot \\ln x + x^{2} \\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\ln x)) \\\\\n&= y \\cdot ((2x) \\cdot \\ln x + x^{2} \\cdot (\\frac{1}{x})) \\\\\n&= y(2x\\ln x + x) \\\\\n&= xy(2\\ln x + 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186192345 :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{4x-y}{x+y^2}$, evaluate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ at the point $(2,-1)$."] [17592186192345 :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x$, treating all other variables as constants.\n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{4x - y}{x + y^{2}}) &= (\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4x - y) \\cdot (x + y^{2}) - (4x - y) \\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x + y^{2}))/((x + y^{2})^{2}) \\\\\n&= (4 \\cdot (x + y^{2}) - (4x - y) \\cdot 1)/((x + y^{2})^{2}) \\\\\n&= (4x + 4y^{2} - 4x + y)/((x + y^{2})^{2}) \\\\\n&= (4y^{2} + y)/((x + y^{2})^{2})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,-1)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x} \\mid _{(2,-1)} &= (4(-1)^{2} + (-1))/((2 + (-1)^{2})^{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{4 - 1}{3^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186192335 :question/problem "For the function $g(x,y,z) = 2 (x + 1)e^z+ yz$, evaluate $\\dfrac{\\partial g}{\\partial z}$ at $(1,1,1)$."] [17592186192335 :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $z$, treating all other variables as constants.\n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{∂g}{∂z} &= \\frac{∂}{∂z}(2(x + 1)e^{z} + yz) \\\\\n&= \\frac{∂}{∂z}(2(x + 1)e^{z}) + \\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz) \\\\\n&= 2(x + 1)\\frac{∂}{∂z}(e^{z}) + \\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz) \\\\\n&= 2(x + 1)e^{z} + y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,1,1)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{∂g}{∂z} \\mid _{(1, 1, 1)} &= 2(1 + 1)e^{1} + 1 \\\\\n&= 4e + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186190994 17592186190995 17592186190996 17592186190997 17592186190998 17592186191671 17592186191672 17592186191673 17592186191674 17592186191675 17592186191677 17592186191678 17592186191679 17592186191680 17592186191681] "immutable_fields" [[17592186190993 :answer-field/correct] [17592186190993 :answer-field/id] [17592186190993 :answer-field/key] [17592186190993 :answer-field/type] [17592186191670 :answer-field/correct] [17592186191670 :answer-field/id] [17592186191670 :answer-field/key] [17592186191670 :answer-field/type] [17592186191676 :answer-field/correct] [17592186191676 :answer-field/id] [17592186191676 :answer-field/key] [17592186191676 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
